{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791642416,"nonce":"BZWaQ7wKANm7CFnuVqT/uOX/ghA=","title":"text_input rebuilds its content on every keystroke, click and drag","message":"`TextInput` is a Stateful\u003cTextFieldState\u003e whose `build_content` derives everything from the mutex-held `TextInputData`: the shown text (value, masked, or placeholder), its colour, the horizontal scroll offset (`left(-scroll_offset_x)`), the cursor (`left(cursor_x)`, a canvas with blink state), the selection rectangles, and the border for idle / hovered / focused / disabled. Every handler mutates `TextInputData` and then calls `refresh_stateful`, which rebuilds that content: per keystroke, per click, per drag step. It is also the last widget that queues subtree rebuilds (combobox's tests have to let them through), and number_input / input_otp in cn rebuild around it to push a formatted value back into its buffer.\n\n\nKeep `TextInputData` as the authority (`SharedTextInputData` is read across the codebase, `.lock().value` included) and add one revision signal per input, bumped wherever a handler now calls `refresh_stateful`. The content is built once and binds to computeds that read the revision and then the data:\n\n- shown text: `Text::bound` over a computed string (value, masked form, or placeholder); colour likewise.\n- scroll offset and cursor position: bound `transform` (translate), not `left`, so neither needs layout.\n- selection: a bound translate and width.\n- border and background per state: computeds over the visual state, which the focus / hover handlers already keep in `TextInputData.visual`.\n- cursor blink: unchanged (canvas reads `cursor_state`).\n\nThen text_area on the same pattern (multi-line: per-line spans), then cn number_input / input_otp, which can write the value through the data and bump the revision instead of rebuilding.\n\nRisks to test for: IME composition, masked input, centred alignment (number / OTP), scroll-into-view of the cursor, mobile focus (`focus_text_input_deferred`), long-press selection.","files":null}]}